OL,3,GNEWSAFamilies 'heartbroken' as grave
OL,4,Adecorations binned
OL,5,
OL,6,FFamilies say they are "disgusted" and
OL,7,F"heartbroken" after ornaments, flowers
OL,8,Fand teddys were removed from their
OL,9,Floved ones' graves and dumped in a
OL,10,Fwheelie bin.
OL,12,FMany of the items had adorned the
OL,13,Fgraves at St Martin's Church in Hayton,
OL,14,Fnear Pocklington, for several years.
OL,15,FRelatives believe they were broken and
OL,16,Fbinned by church wardens.
OL,18,FFaye Smith, whose son James died at
OL,19,Fbirth in 2003, said a teddy which had
OL,20,Fbeen at the side of his grave for 23
OL,21,Fyears had been taken away, causing her
OL,22,Fto "relive the grief again".
OL,23,APub: 19-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
